# FFmpeg rules for VAT

Status legend: [VERIFIED] = run successfully on synthetic test data (ffmpeg 6.1, libx264, Linux) before this spec was written.
[UNVERIFIED] = design proposal, must be proven by a test before relying on it.

## Invocation
- `ProcessStartInfo`: `UseShellExecute=false`, `CreateNoWindow=true`, redirect stdout+stderr, UTF-8 encodings, use `ArgumentList`.
- Read stdout AND stderr concurrently (avoid pipe deadlock). Keep the last 25 non-progress lines for error reports.
- Run every job with `WorkingDirectory = <per-job temp dir>`. Therefore EVERY input/output path passed to ffmpeg MUST be absolute.
  (Bug found in prototype: a relative output path was resolved inside the temp dir and then deleted.)
- Per-job temp dir contains `sub.ass` and optional `fonts/`. Delete it in `finally`.
- Reference the ASS file by RELATIVE name: `ass=filename=sub.ass` (and `:fontsdir=fonts`). Never pass absolute Windows paths inside a
  filter (drive-letter colon and backslashes need fragile escaping).
- Always add: `-y -hide_banner -loglevel warning -nostdin`. For renders also `-progress pipe:1 -nostats`; parse `out_time_us`
  (microseconds) / total duration for percent.
- Write to `<final>.mp4.part` with `-f mp4`, then move over the final name on success. On failure/cancel delete the `.part`.
- Cancel = kill the process tree, then delete `.part`.

## Timing
- D (job duration) = duration of the FIRST AUDIO STREAM of the source (fallback: container duration). Output gets `-t D`.
- Only `-map 0:a:0` for audio. Never map audio of backgrounds (their voice must never appear).
- Everything is normalized to canvas WxH and fps F with `fps=F` on each input so the graph is constant frame rate.

## Baseline filter graph [VERIFIED]
Inputs: `0`=source (audio only), `1..K`=background segments, then avatar image, then soundwave.
```
color=c=black:s=WxH:r=F:d=D,format=gbrp[base]
[k:v]trim=duration=SEG,setpts=PTS-STARTPTS,fps=F,
   scale=w='trunc(max(W/iw,H/ih)*iw*S/2)*2':h='trunc(max(W/iw,H/ih)*ih*S/2)*2':flags=bicubic,
   crop=w='min(iw,W)':h='min(ih,H)',pad=W:H:(ow-iw)/2:(oh-ih)/2:color=black,setsar=1[sK]
[s0][s1]...concat=n=K:v=1:a=0[bgcat]            (K==1: [s0]copy[bgcat])
[bgcat]format=rgba,colorchannelmixer=aa=OPACITY[bga]
[base][bga]overlay=eof_action=repeat:format=gbrp[L1]
[A:v]fps=F,trim=duration=D,setpts=PTS-STARTPTS,format=rgba,scale=w=AW:h=AH:force_original_aspect_ratio=decrease[av]
[L1][av]overlay=x='EXPR':y='EXPR':eof_action=repeat:format=gbrp[L2]
[Wv:v]fps=F,trim=duration=D,setpts=PTS-STARTPTS,format=rgba,scale=w=WW:h=-2:flags=bicubic[wv]
[L2][wv]overlay=x='EXPR':y='EXPR':eof_action=repeat:format=gbrp[L3]
[L3]ass=filename=sub.ass[L4]
[L4]scale=out_color_matrix=bt709:out_range=tv:flags=accurate_rnd+full_chroma_int,format=yuv420p[vout]
```
- S = background scale factor. "cover" mode: 1.0 fills the canvas exactly; 1.5 = 150 % of that (centre-cropped).
- Segment durations: all full length except the last, which is `remaining`. Backgrounds are chained by the planner, not by ffmpeg.
- Opacity over black was measured: mean luma ratio 0.604 for OPACITY=0.6 (expected 0.6).
- Overlay `x`/`y` expressions use `W,H` (main) and `w,h` (overlay); they may be negative or exceed the canvas (overflow is cropped by overlay).
- Avatar is a single still frame (no `-loop`): `format=rgba,scale=...` once, then `overlay=eof_action=repeat`.
- Soundwave: `-stream_loop -1`; baked cache (scale + lumakey, qtrle argb) is used on the CPU graph. 720p black-key wave still uses `chromakey_cuda` on the original file.
- Driver input is audio-only: `-vn -sn -dn` before `-i` so a long source does not demux unused video.
- Soundwave with black background instead of alpha: insert `lumakey=threshold=0:tolerance=T:softness=T` after `format=rgba` (T ~ 0.12-0.15) [VERIFIED].
- Soundwave with alpha: QuickTime `qtrle`/ProRes 4444 `.mov` decoded to rgba works [VERIFIED].
- Layer opacity other than 1.0 on avatar/wave: append `colorchannelmixer=aa=X` after `format=rgba` [VERIFIED for wave].
- Order of layers in the template (bottom -> top) = order of overlays.

## Encoders
- CPU [VERIFIED]: `-c:v libx264 -preset medium -crf Q -profile:v high`
- NVIDIA [UNVERIFIED, no GPU on the machine where this was written]: `-c:v h264_nvenc -preset p5 -rc vbr -cq Q -b:v 0 -profile:v high`
- Detect NVENC by a tiny test encode (`-f lavfi -i color=c=black:s=256x256:d=0.2 -c:v h264_nvenc -f null -`); exit code 0 => usable; else libx264.
  Cache the detection result per ffmpeg path.
- Tags: `-colorspace bt709 -color_primaries bt709 -color_trc bt709 -color_range tv -movflags +faststart`
- Audio: filter `[0:a]atrim,asetpts,aformat[aout]` then `-map [aout]`. Do not use `-map 0:a:0` (ffmpeg 7 mux queue overflow on long files).

## Preview frame [VERIFIED]
Build the SAME graph with D reduced to `t + 0.5`, then output-side `-ss t -frames:v 1`, finish with
`scale=800:-2:flags=bicubic,format=rgb24[vout]` and write PNG. Do not map audio.

## Cache (freeze) [UNVERIFIED - must be proven in the cache milestone]
Idea: prepare each background ONCE at canvas size with the opacity baked in (opacity over black == multiply RGB by opacity:
`format=gbrp,colorchannelmixer=rr=O:gg=O:bb=O`), store as H.264 with identical parameters, then feed the render ONE input via the
concat demuxer (`-f concat -safe 0 -i list.txt`) and use it directly as the base layer (`trim=duration=D`). This avoids opening
dozens of inputs for 30-40 minute videos. Prove: equal look to the baseline (luma ratio test), identical duration, faster.

## Text / ASS [VERIFIED]
- Generate an ASS file per job (PlayResX/Y = canvas, `WrapStyle: 2`, `ScaledBorderAndShadow: yes`), position each line with
  `{\anN\pos(x,y)}`, wrap by inserting `\N` yourself. Colors are `&H00BBGGRR`.
- Time format `H:MM:SS.cc`. Strip HTML-like tags from SRT text. Strip emoji from titles taken from file names.
- Font must be an installed font family name (or a font file copied into `fonts/` and the family name typed by the user).

## Pitfalls already found
1. Relative output path + custom cwd => file lost. Always absolute.
2. Emoji in file names are fine when passed via `ArgumentList`; but never put such names inside a filter string.
3. SRT files may be UTF-8 with BOM; also try UTF-16 and CP1258 before Latin-1.
4. `pad` after `crop` is required, otherwise scale < 1.0 leaves the wrong size.
5. Source videos are shorter/longer than backgrounds: NEVER assume; the planner chains backgrounds until `total >= D - 0.02`.
6. Concat of segments needs equal fps/size/sar: hence `fps=F`, `setsar=1`, and `pad` on every segment.
7. Background cache key uses `DurationFull`. Encode the full clip, then trim to D at render time. Encoding only the first job's D poisons later longer jobs (`-shortest` cuts them).
8. After `progress=end`, `+faststart` may still rewrite a large file on HDD. Only kill ffmpeg if the `.part` size is unchanged for 15s.
9. Prefer writing `.part` on the SSD (`%LocalAppData%\VideoAutoTool\out-tmp`) then copy once to the HDD destination.
10. Never `string.Replace` the job duration into the filter graph. `4`/`20`/`25`/`420` also appear in `yuv420p` and `fps=25`. Build the graph with the clip duration instead.
